<title>PORTUGAL: Escudo holds firm on mark after rate cut.</title>
<headline>Escudo holds firm on mark after rate cut.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The escudo showed no reaction to the rate cut by the Bank of Portugal as the reduction had been discounted, traders said.</p>
<p>It was trading at 99.96/99 to the mark against its opening 100.04/08.</p>
<p>The Bank of Portugal cut 20 basis points from its repurchase rate to 6.30 percent and lowered its drain rate, the level at which it absorbs market funds, to 5.8 percent from 6.2 percent previously.</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
